00:43:32.976 --> 00:43:36.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it can't be that
friendly anymore.

00:43:36.413 --> 00:43:37.915
It just can't be.

00:43:37.915 --> 00:43:40.450
So you kind of know, hmm,
he's running for office.

00:43:40.450 --> 00:43:42.986
This is not the end of
our personal friendship,

00:43:42.986 --> 00:43:45.855 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it's definitely gonna
be on pause for a long time.

00:43:45.855 --> 00:43:49.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then my second
example is Donald Trump,

00:43:49.660 --> 00:43:53.463
when he was a celebrity
and, you know, on TV,

00:43:53.463 --> 00:43:55.599
he used to come on Fox, he
was great. He always raided.

00:43:55.599 --> 00:43:56.800
He was fun to talk to.

00:43:56.800 --> 00:43:58.235
He invited me to a couple

00:43:58.235 --> 00:44:01.204 align:start position:0%
of these "Celebrity Apprentice"
things, which I went to.

00:44:01.204 --> 00:44:03.840 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was always very gregarious,
you know, he'd walk in,

00:44:03.840 --> 00:44:06.310
he'd give you the big hug
and kiss and like, ah.

00:44:07.244 --> 00:44:09.412
It was tough not to like Trump.

00:44:09.412 --> 00:44:12.149
And then he decided
to run for president

00:44:12.149 --> 00:44:15.085
and he invited me to
go down to Mar-a-Lago.

00:44:15.085 --> 00:44:16.619
you've gotta see it.

00:44:16.619 --> 00:44:17.887
It's so beautiful. Sent me
all these pictures of it.

00:44:17.887 --> 00:44:21.458
I was like, hell no, I'm
not going to Mar-a-Lago,

00:44:21.458 --> 00:44:22.793 align:start size:81% position:19%
the guy is running
for president.

00:44:22.793 --> 00:44:24.260
Guess what?

00:44:24.260 --> 00:44:26.930
A lot of other journalists
did not make the same choice.

00:44:26.930 --> 00:44:30.434
Then he found out that I
was going on a girls trip

00:44:30.434 --> 00:44:32.903
and we were gonna stay at Trump,

00:44:32.903 --> 00:44:37.975
I know one of his hotels,
and he tried to pay for it.

00:44:39.109 --> 00:44:40.076
He reached out to say,
where are you staying?

00:44:40.076 --> 00:44:41.144 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Ooh.
- I'll take care of it.

00:44:41.144 --> 00:44:42.412
Oh, very nice, right?

00:44:42.412 --> 00:44:44.181 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Ooh yeah.
- In quotes. It's not nice.

00:44:44.181 --> 00:44:45.849
And I said, absolutely not.

00:44:45.849 --> 00:44:48.351
Thank you very much Mr. Trump,
we'll pay for our own hotel.

00:44:48.351 --> 00:44:49.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I said to
Abby, my assistant,

00:44:49.719 --> 00:44:51.655
make sure you hold
onto the records.

00:44:51.655 --> 00:44:52.922
You know, like they,

00:44:52.922 --> 00:44:54.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is what
politicians try to do

00:44:54.525 --> 00:44:56.292
and humans try to do it too.

00:44:56.292 --> 00:44:58.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's one thing for
Donald Trump's celebrity

00:44:58.829 --> 00:45:00.664
to try to woo me
over to liking him.

00:45:00.664 --> 00:45:02.365
That's less fraught.

00:45:02.365 --> 00:45:05.902
But politician Donald Trump
has to receive a hard no

00:45:05.902 --> 00:45:07.337
in response to all
those overtures.

00:45:07.337 --> 00:45:09.039
And Dave, that night,

00:45:09.039 --> 00:45:11.908
I went on to the debate
stage August 6th, 2015

00:45:11.908 --> 00:45:13.877
and asked him that
very hard question.

00:45:13.877 --> 00:45:15.112 align:start size:81% position:19%
There were lots
of hard questions,

00:45:15.112 --> 00:45:17.047
just that one that
everybody remembers.

00:45:17.047 --> 00:45:20.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, what I
had behind my notes,

00:45:20.183 --> 00:45:22.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
in addition to my outline
and my fact checks,

00:45:22.252 --> 00:45:23.487
which are 10 deep,

00:45:23.487 --> 00:45:26.056
and I was ready to back
up everything I asked.

00:45:26.056 --> 00:45:29.293
I had the receipts from
that Trump hotel visit

00:45:29.293 --> 00:45:32.196 align:start position:0%
and my rejection of his
invitation to go to Mar-a-Lago.

00:45:32.196 --> 00:45:33.363 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Ooh.
- Because-

00:45:33.363 --> 00:45:34.164 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You were ready.
- I didn't want anybody

00:45:34.164 --> 00:45:35.398
using that against me.

00:45:35.398 --> 00:45:37.501
Same as I'll have to do
it to Vivek Ramaswamy

00:45:37.501 --> 00:45:38.869 align:start size:84% position:16%
if he ever tries to
say you did, you know?

00:45:38.869 --> 00:45:42.072
Like it's just, it
gets very complicated

00:45:42.072 --> 00:45:44.674 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you have to cover
them objectively.

00:45:44.674 --> 00:45:47.777
So I think, you know, you
either have to choose,

00:45:47.777 --> 00:45:50.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
or you have to just be
very open about your bias.

00:45:50.413 --> 00:45:52.249
You know, like, I know
you're a DeSantis guy,

00:45:52.249 --> 00:45:55.986
you've been open about that,
so I think you're okay there.

00:45:55.986 --> 00:45:58.221
But if you have too many
of those with politicians,

00:45:58.221 --> 00:46:00.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
it can get dicey quickly.
- Yeah.

00:46:00.123 --> 00:46:02.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
And for sure, you know, for
just from, for my perspective,

00:46:02.826 --> 00:46:05.361
like the politician version,
I don't have that much of it.

00:46:05.361 --> 00:46:07.731 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, I played
basketball with Ted Cruz

00:46:07.731 --> 00:46:08.765
or I played video
games with him.

00:46:08.765 --> 00:46:10.033
We're like some of that stuff,

00:46:10.033 --> 00:46:11.501
but we're not like
friends like that.

00:46:11.501 --> 00:46:13.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think for me, it's more
like the pundit class

00:46:13.269 --> 00:46:15.506
where I see guys that
are like kind of doing

00:46:15.506 --> 00:46:16.973
what we do and then they kind of

00:46:16.973 --> 00:46:20.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
go completely off the deep
end and I'm like, ugh,

00:46:20.010 --> 00:46:21.578
do I have to call you out?

00:46:21.578 --> 00:46:23.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's more that I
think for me than the-

00:46:23.413 --> 00:46:25.082
- Yes, well you have, and
the answer is yes, you do.

00:46:25.082 --> 00:46:26.749
You you have to.
- You do. No, I do.

00:46:26.749 --> 00:46:29.286
And like you, I have my,
my short friend list so.

00:46:30.086 --> 00:46:30.921
- I've gotta tell you one other.

00:46:30.921 --> 00:46:31.822
- Yeah, yeah.

00:46:32.856 --> 00:46:36.927 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So couple years
back, there's this guy,

00:46:36.927 --> 00:46:38.494
his name is Carlos Watson,

00:46:38.494 --> 00:46:40.163
he invites me to go
on his YouTube show.

00:46:40.163 --> 00:46:41.498
I never heard of Carlos Watson.

00:46:41.498 --> 00:46:43.032
I'm like, who is he?

00:46:43.032 --> 00:46:44.668
Abby's like, I don't know, but
you're sandwiched in between,

00:46:44.668 --> 00:46:47.738
it was like LeBron
James and Bill Gates.

00:46:47.738 --> 00:46:49.806
So I'm like, who is this guy?

00:46:49.806 --> 00:46:52.342
Like, he's got access
to some very big names

00:46:52.342 --> 00:46:54.077
and I don't remember
what the forum was on,

00:46:54.077 --> 00:46:55.012
but it was on a big day.

00:46:55.012 --> 00:46:56.246
It was like election night.

00:46:56.246 --> 00:46:58.047
And so I'm like,
okay, I'll do it.

00:46:58.047 --> 00:46:59.216
She's like, he's got
all these followers.

00:46:59.216 --> 00:47:00.216
His show's very successful.

00:47:00.216 --> 00:47:01.651
Okay so I did it.

00:47:01.651 --> 00:47:04.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
Carlos was a perfect
gentleman, very nice guy,

00:47:04.287 --> 00:47:05.155
solid interviewer.

00:47:05.155 --> 00:47:06.656
Had a good time.

00:47:06.656 --> 00:47:08.892 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then I went on a couple
more times, fine.

00:47:08.892 --> 00:47:10.159 align:start size:84% position:16%
Eventually I'm
like, you know what?

00:47:10.159 --> 00:47:11.294
I launched my show, I'm
like, I'll have him on.

00:47:11.294 --> 00:47:12.562
Had him on very nice.

00:47:12.562 --> 00:47:14.531
Kind of cagey about like
what his background was.

00:47:14.531 --> 00:47:15.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
He didn't wanna
talk about his life,

00:47:15.799 --> 00:47:16.733
but that's fine.

00:47:16.733 --> 00:47:18.001
Some people are like that.

00:47:18.001 --> 00:47:20.270
Then he wanted me to
go to his Ozy Fest.

00:47:20.270 --> 00:47:21.738
It was like a, you know,

00:47:21.738 --> 00:47:23.373
like one of those media
things like Jordan has,

00:47:23.373 --> 00:47:24.340
you know, everybody goes.

00:47:24.340 --> 00:47:25.275
Okay.

00:47:25.275 --> 00:47:26.509
I'm like, I don't know.

00:47:26.509 --> 00:47:27.977
Then I see the list
of everybody's going.

00:47:27.977 --> 00:47:30.614
It's like all these amazing
names, people I respect,

00:47:30.614 --> 00:47:31.548
people I know.

00:47:32.682 --> 00:47:35.385
I'm like, all right, you
know, I'll look into it.

00:47:35.385 --> 00:47:36.753
And the next thing I see,

00:47:37.887 --> 00:47:42.860
Carlos and Ozy Media are
under SEC investigation

00:47:43.660 --> 00:47:46.129
for impersonating a YouTube CEO,

00:47:46.129 --> 00:47:49.899
the officer, the
chief executive, or
COO of the company,

00:47:49.899 --> 00:47:51.868
as Goldman Sachs was
trying to figure out

00:47:51.868 --> 00:47:54.404 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it was going to give
Ozy another business loan

00:47:54.404 --> 00:47:55.872
and wanted to kick the tires

00:47:55.872 --> 00:47:57.874 align:start size:88% position:13%
and see if those YouTube
numbers were real.

00:47:57.874 --> 00:48:00.010
Well, instead of connecting
them with the actual YouTube,

00:48:00.010 --> 00:48:03.246 align:start size:84% position:16%
his CFO faked being
the YouTube executive,

00:48:03.246 --> 00:48:04.815
lied about their numbers.

00:48:04.815 --> 00:48:06.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
The whole thing
came crashing down.

00:48:06.783 --> 00:48:09.386
It was a house of cards
that was all made up.

00:48:09.386 --> 00:48:10.987
The YouTube numbers were fake.

00:48:10.987 --> 00:48:14.124 align:start size:97% position:3%
Carlos pretty soon
thereafter was under arrest.

00:48:14.124 --> 00:48:15.658
The CFO was under arrest.

00:48:15.658 --> 00:48:17.060
Ozy Fest was off.

00:48:17.060 --> 00:48:19.395
And I'm thinking to myself,

00:48:19.395 --> 00:48:22.532
it don't become chummy
with any of these people.

00:48:22.532 --> 00:48:24.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I went out on
the air and I'm like,

00:48:24.367 --> 00:48:26.936
I've got something to tell
you members of my audience,

00:48:26.936 --> 00:48:29.239
this guy who we had
on not too long ago

00:48:29.239 --> 00:48:31.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
and celebrated his
independent entrepreneurship,

00:48:31.774 --> 00:48:35.044
he's a fraud according to the
government and several others.

00:48:35.044 --> 00:48:37.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyway, it's just the
whole business is fraught.

00:48:37.514 --> 00:48:38.981
And if you become
friends with me,

00:48:38.981 --> 00:48:41.785 align:start position:0%
there's a 90% chance you're
gonna wind up being a fraudster

00:48:41.785 --> 00:48:44.254
'cause that's happened to me
over and over, Dave Rubin.

00:48:44.254 --> 00:48:46.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Excuse me, Megyn
Kelly, we are friends.

00:48:46.723 --> 00:48:49.492 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have shared
tequila many times,

00:48:49.492 --> 00:48:51.794
and I am not a fraud.

00:48:51.794 --> 00:48:54.263
And you are not a,
you, you actually,

00:48:54.263 --> 00:48:55.732 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know I can say nice things
about you all the time,

00:48:55.732 --> 00:48:57.234 align:start size:84% position:16%
but when people
always ask me, Dave,

00:48:57.234 --> 00:48:59.302
who do you watch to make
any sense to any of this?

00:48:59.302 --> 00:49:00.671
It's like, it's basically you.

00:49:00.671 --> 00:49:02.472
It's you and Jordan for me.

00:49:02.472 --> 00:49:03.674 align:start size:72% position:28%
- And-
- Thank you.

00:49:03.674 --> 00:49:05.842 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I thank you for
doing this as always.

00:49:05.842 --> 00:49:07.377
And are you gonna come to,

00:49:07.377 --> 00:49:09.145
why don't you come down to
Miami for the next debate?

00:49:09.145 --> 00:49:12.482 align:start position:0%
We can have tequila and you
can yell at the the moderators.

00:49:12.482 --> 00:49:14.017 align:start size:81% position:19%
What do you think?
- Oh, sure.

00:49:14.017 --> 00:49:16.453
Oh, I'd love to reconnect
with my old pals from NBC.

00:49:16.453 --> 00:49:19.189 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll do it if you and I can
sit behind them with tomatoes.

00:49:19.189 --> 00:49:20.691
- Yes, that can be arranged.

00:49:20.691 --> 00:49:23.060
- Bitter party of one, no two.

00:49:23.060 --> 00:49:24.294
- We're more of an orange state.

00:49:24.294 --> 00:49:25.963
We can throw some
oranges at 'em.

